We're implementing GitHub issue #801 in the family-tree repo (React+TS frontend, FastAPI backend, but this issue is frontend-only).

## Issue #801
Title: "Documents tab: single click on a document should collapse/expand it"

Body:
In the member sheet's Documents section (`frontend/src/components/shared/member-sheet/MemberDocuments.tsx`), each document is rendered fully expanded — title, date, description, and the attached file list (`DocumentFileList`) are always visible. With several documents on a member, this section gets long and hard to scan.

Expected behavior: Clicking anywhere on a document's row (outside the edit/delete buttons) should toggle a collapsed/expanded state for that document — collapsed shows just the title (and maybe date), expanded shows the full description and file list, similar to how other collapsible sections in the app work (see `RecordSectionCard`, which `MemberDocuments` already renders inside, for the pattern to reuse).

Suggested approach:
- Add per-document collapsed state (e.g. a `Set<string>` of expanded document IDs, or default-collapsed vs default-expanded — worth confirming with design/UX) in `MemberDocuments.tsx`.
- Add an `onClick` on the row container that toggles the state, taking care not to trigger when the click originates from the Edit/Delete buttons (`e.stopPropagation()` on those buttons, as is likely already needed).
- Hide/show the description + `DocumentFileList` block based on the collapsed state.

Acceptance Criteria:
- [ ] Clicking a document row (not its buttons) toggles showing/hiding its description and file list
- [ ] Edit and delete buttons still work without triggering the collapse toggle
- [ ] Keyboard/a11y: row should be reachable and toggleable via keyboard too (e.g. `role="button"` + `tabIndex`/`onKeyDown`, or a dedicated disclosure control)
- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md` entry under `## [Unreleased]`

Relevant files: `frontend/src/components/shared/member-sheet/MemberDocuments.tsx`, `frontend/src/components/shared/member-sheet/DocumentFiles.tsx`, `frontend/src/components/shared/member-sheet/RecordSectionCard.tsx`

## What I already know (don't re-derive, just use it)

Current `MemberDocuments.tsx` (full contents, 142 lines):

```tsx
